## Overview
Root-cause check: the critique does not change the root cause. M0 is still about making `@reigh/editor-sdk` a portable SDK boundary by removing SDK-to-host imports and proving an external package-like consumer can compile and evaluate the SDK without repo aliases or video-editor internals. The critique does sharpen the target in two places: timeline extraction must be split into worker-sized domain seams, and the `src/sdk/**` boundary must explicitly account for tests because existing SDK tests currently deep-import host runtime repositories while the current guard excludes tests.

This revision keeps the North Star intact. Production SDK files must never import host internals. Files that remain under `src/sdk/**`, including tests, must also stop statically importing `src/tools/video-editor/**` or `@/tools/video-editor/**` unless they are deliberate guard fixtures isolated outside the real SDK tree. Host-coupled SDK tests should either move to a host-owned test location or be rewritten with SDK-local fakes so the directory itself stops normalizing host leakage.

M0 remains a bridge milestone. It preserves `@reigh/editor-sdk` as the public barrel, keeps existing public exports compatible, and creates SDK-owned modules only for portable contracts and pure values needed to break host imports. It does not yet perform the later core/video/family split beyond the scoped rendering, timeline, asset, and config contract modules required for portability.

## Phase 0: Baseline Truth

